==English==

===Etymology===
From a 1990 article by Morning Glory Zell-Ravenheart, "A Bouquet of Lovers", from {{m|en|poly-}} (from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πολύς||many}}) + {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|amor||love}} + {{m|en|-ous}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having [[relationship]]s with multiple [[partner]]s, with the knowledge and consent of all involved; engaging in [[polyamory]].
# Open to having such relationships, regardless of one's experience or current practices.

====Alternative forms====
